cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NeuroPyHLS, please cite it as below."
title: "NeuroPyHLS: high-level synthesis of neural-signal algorithms directly from Python to Verilog"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Monge
    given-names: Manuel
    email: manuel@openic.org
    affiliation: OpenIC
repository-code: "https://github.com/openic-org/NeuroPyHLS"
url: "https://openic-org.github.io/NeuroPyHLS/"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0.dev0
date-released: "2026-10-30"
abstract: >-
  NeuroPyHLS is a high-level synthesis compiler that lowers neural-signal algorithms written in
  Python directly to Verilog, without a C++ step. A baseline flow through HLS C++ and Bambu or
  Vitis HLS is used to verify it and compare against it.
keywords:
  - high-level synthesis
  - Python to Verilog
  - FPGA
  - ASIC
  - neural signal processing
  - electrophysiology
